            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sentence": 55,
        "en": "Having discussed ways to sample behaviour in research, we are now moving onto another issue, that is, what researchers should do to record behaviour as it occurs, that is whether researchers are active or passive in recording behaviour.",
        "at": "what researchers should do",
        "zh": [
          "讨论完研究中如何进行行为取样后，我们接下来转向另一个问题：",
          "研究人员应如何实时记录行为，也就是他们在记录时是主动介入还是被动观察。"
        ],
        "true_cut_word_anchors": [
          {
            "at": "what researchers should do",
            "char": 102,
            "actual_first_word": "what",
            "actual_first_word_window": [
              395.67,
              395.75
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sentence": 59,
        "en": "In participant observation, observers, that is researchers, play a dual role: They observe people’s behaviour and they participate actively in the situation they are observing.",
        "at": "They observe people’s behaviour",
        "zh": [
          "在参与式观察中，观察者，也就是研究人员，承担双重角色：",
          "既观察人们的行为，也积极参与所观察的情境。"
        ],
        "true_cut_word_anchors": [
          {
            "at": "They observe people’s behaviour",
            "char": 78,
            "actual_first_word": "They",
            "actual_first_word_window": [
              433.91,
              433.99
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sentence": 60,
        "en": "If individuals who are being observed know that the observer is present to collect information about their behaviour, this is undisguised participant observation.",
        "at": "this is undisguised participant",
        "zh": [
          "如果被观察者知道，观察者在场是为了收集他们的行为信息，",
          "这就属于公开的参与式观察。"
        ],
        "true_cut_word_anchors": [
          {
            "at": "this is undisguised participant",
            "char": 118,
            "actual_first_word": "this",
            "actual_first_word_window": [
